Notebooks

Two Google Colab notebooks reproduce the results of the article. Run the cells in order.

Notebook	Content	Outputs
01_blind_zone_pipeline.ipynb	Main pipeline on BitFraud: strata, address-history rule and history refresh, anomaly detectors, consolidation score, review workload, walk-forward validation, budget routing, remedies and enriched features.	results/02_rule_refresh to results/08_routing, results/11_regime to results/14_enriched, results/validate.json
02_elliptic_blind_zone.ipynb	Blind-zone analysis and expert retraining on Elliptic++ (CPU only).	results/09_elliptic_blind, results/10_elliptic_refresh
Setup
Place the BitFraud files (Zenodo record) under ROOT/01_data/ and the Elliptic++ files under ROOT/elliptic_plus_plus/.
Set ROOT in the notebooks to your project folder. The notebooks use /content/drive/MyDrive/bitcoin_snapshots_project (a Google Drive path in Colab).
Outputs are written to ROOT/05_results/bz/; the copy in results/ is the one used in the article.

Each section title of the first notebook names the output folder it writes. Seeds are fixed in the code. Dependencies are listed in requirements.txt at the root of the repository.
